===

title: ExplainQs
---
You: "Ah...well... 'Would you sacrifice one person to save many
people?' is a common philosophy question. It comes from the
trolley problem and shows what someone values,"

Faust grows quiet, thinking carefully.

Faust: "Ahh...I see, that makes sense,"

You nod, satisfied.

===

title: AskWhat
---
You: "What's wrong with them?"

You glance at your questions. They are standard philosophical
topics, but not everyone dwells on them like you do.

Faust: "Nothing, nothing. They're fine,"

He answers quickly, clearing his throat. That only confuses you
more.

===

title: Defend
---
You: "Cringe?"

You repeat, surprised.

You: "Last time I checked, I was the Philosophy student, not
you. These are very common questions,"

Your patience begins to thin.

Faust raises his hands defensively.

Faust: "Woah okay. Sorry, my fault. You're the one asking the
questions, I get it,"

It doesn't fully address your frustration, but you decide to
move on.

===
